📖 Description

This project is a relational database system for managing an online bookstore. It demonstrates the design and implementation of SQL queries to handle books, customers, and orders efficiently.

The project includes:

Database Schema:

Books → stores book details (ID, title, stock, etc.)

Customers → stores customer information

Orders_Books → manages book orders and their quantities

Key Features:

Track available stock for each book

Calculate ordered quantities and remaining stock dynamically

Generate reports using JOIN, GROUP BY, and aggregate functions

Handle edge cases with COALESCE for missing data

Dataset:

Sample data is provided in CSV format (Books.csv, Customers.csv, Orders.csv)

Can be imported into MySQL or any relational DBMS

Learning Outcomes:

Practice SQL concepts (JOIN, GROUP BY, ORDER BY, aggregate functions)

Work with real-world bookstore management use case

Understand database normalization and query optimization
